The Perl port refuses every item with a .njk file (perl/lib/Skilletor/Render.pm build croaks, "renders nothing"; Engine.pm holds such items back with a warning; Skilletor.pm resolve_* throw Skilletor::Error::Unsupported). The reference src/render.ts renders them with nunjucks: a loader confined to the item source root (an include leaving it is RenderError "template escapes source root: <name>"), autoescape false, throwOnUndefined true, env.render(file, context), errors wrapped as "<file>: <message>", a template passes its executable bit to what it renders.

Engine: Text::Nunjucks, the 1:1 Perl port of Nunjucks 3.2.4 (local checkout /home/getty/dev/p5-text-nunjucks, https://github.com/Getty/p5-text-nunjucks, not on CPAN yet). The loader is a subclass of Text::Nunjucks::Loader (a bare get_source object is an open decision there, its k94). Nothing in p5-text-nunjucks is changed from here: deviations from what render.ts needs are reported (template, node output, Perl output), not worked around.

Done:
- perl/cpanfile requires Text::Nunjucks; the Perl test command (CLAUDE.md, perl/README.md) puts the checkout lib on PERL5LIB.
- Render.pm renders .njk like render.ts; Engine.pm syncs templated items (renders-empty skip included) like the reference.
- conformance/cases/09-templates meets the shared expected/; its expected.perl/ and engines.perl block go (it is the only case with one).
- Parity tests (Perl vs node) cover a template with an include, an undefined variable and an escaping include.
- Perl suite green; TypeScript suite untouched and green.
- POD (Render.pm, Engine.pm, Skilletor.pm), perl/README.md, docs/perl.md, conformance/README.md say what is true now; perl/Changes entry.
- Report: what CI (.github/workflows/perl.yml, cpanm --installdeps) needs until Text::Nunjucks is on CPAN.

